sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015) & Chirat et al. (2013) hierarchical mollusc aperture spine folding and fractal frond serration faithfully reproduces Murex pecten (Venus comb murex) & Chicoreus ramosus (ramose murex / Muricidae) morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Murex pecten (Venus comb murex) & Chicoreus ramosus (ramose murex / Muricidae) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py; output: docs/media/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_comparison.png; organism: Murex pecten (Venus comb murex) & Chicoreus ramosus (ramose murex / Muricidae); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 7e0a58a2882e57518d985e4253c9b131677e4c5f4943a638d01e321b11b48932; artifact_sha256: 1982f3f9822d1bbcf1b1f7746300e631c3f6c1877a192d1178f7c2019f4ea327; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling_reference.json=c73e5d2ac5c13cd5..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/murex_pecten_aperture_specimen.jpg=2f87d4ec30ebec6a..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/paper_citations.bib=fc39398ba54f69e1..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/pass3_koiter_cord_thickness_reference.json=63fdbb231492c336..., datasets/mollusc_aperture_spine_buckling/scout_manifest.json=53cb565add07b28d...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013): the mantle edge is an elastic strip growing against the calcified shell margin; excess growth gamma > gamma_c buckles it with wavelength lambda_1 ~ (E h_1^3 / 3 K_s)^(1/4) set by the mantle thickness and the foundation stiffness, giving comb spines along the siphonal canal of Murex pecten and varix spines in muricids | Moulton, Goriely & Chirat (2015): further growth folds each spine into a Kirchhoff elastica loop that self-contacts into a hollow tube, and thinner secondary/tertiary mantle generations produce the fractal frond cascade k_{i+1}/k_i = (h_i/h_{i+1})^(3/4) of Chicoreus ramosus | Rudraraju et al. (2019): the full problem is a finite-strain morphoelastic shell with surface and volume growth, solved by finite elements | Koiter (1966) and Manor, Hagberg & Meron (2008): the thin-shell energy used for the reduced surface model, and wave-number locking of a pattern-forming system to a spatially periodic forcing (Arnold tongues); reconstructed_in_script: Hierarchical wavenumber law k_i^* = (3 K_s / (E h_i^3))^(1/4); 1-D unilateral fourth-order comb energy minimised by L-BFGS-B at the rounded mode q_mode = 2 pi round(L/lambda_1)/L; parametric omega-loop spine profile with a linear neck-gap law; prescribed 3-stage frond cosines; prescribed 120 deg varix bursts; 10-species cross-taxa table; DoG specimen segmentation (Pass 2) | Pass 3: reduced linearised Koiter/FvK surface w(s,t) on a 192x96 bi-periodic torus (L_s = 67.2 mm, L_t = 24 mm, D = 1, K_0 = (k_1^*)^4) with varix growth window P(t), additive cord ridge forcing, semi-implicit gradient flow + L-BFGS-B relaxation from noise, emergent spine count / cord-intersection registration / ridge tilt; locking-tongue and obliquity sweeps; inverse-WKB h(u) from the specimen spacing profile; graded-rigidity 1-D comb with uniform control; allometric instar series with Brent root beta*; transfer_boundary: The Koiter surface is linearised (no finite membrane strain, flat reference torus, nondimensional D = 1 with outputs labelled mm) and the planar elastica cross-section is not coupled to it; both are separate modules, so the Pass 2 item 1 (3D finite-strain Koiter FE coupling) is addressed only in reduced form | h(s) is inferred from a Murex pecten photograph via inverse WKB (R^2 = 0.29, floor 0.35), not measured by micro-CT, and the species is not the Chicoreus ramosus the Pass 2 item asked for; no Chicoreus specimen is vendored | The 1-D comb spine count 16, the 120 deg varix spacing, the Chicoreus k_2/k_1 = 3.80, the neck-gap delta -3.1059 mm, the specimen CV 0.2092 reference, beta* = 4/3 and the rigid-spine 22.8 deg are prescribed or self-referential and must not be read as validations; does_not_claim: A finite-strain shell FE solution, a numerically integrated Kirchhoff-Clebsch elastica, emergent fractal frond serrations, emergent varix periodicity, measured mantle thickness data for any species, or sourced empirical k_2/k_1 and spine counts for the 10 muricid species]; other sources: On the nonlinear theory of thin elastic shells <https://dwc.knaw.nl/toegangen/digital-library-knaw/?pagetype=publist&search_author=PE00002224>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.09.021>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1209/0295-5075/83/10005>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007213> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.875"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2015-moulton-mollusc-aperture-spine-buckling.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
